From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:38:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 039/207] deepseek: honour TF_DSV41_GRAMMAR=0 for structured
 output

The CUDA model built its grammar masks at every boot and reported structures,
so TF_DSV41_GRAMMAR, which the forward and the replay CLI document, did
nothing. Unset, empty or 1 (the default, as served before) builds the masks on
every rank; 0 leaves them out, so the server refuses required or named tool
calls and structured output and holds no auto request to a grammar; any other
value fails the boot.
---
 zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/cuda_model.zig        |  3 ++-
 zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/grammar_gpu.zig       |  1 +
 zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/grammar_host_test.zig | 12 ++++++++++++
 zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/grammar_rows.zig      |  9 +++++++++
 4 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/cuda_model.zig b/zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/cuda_model.zig
index c3b3a14bb01b75c62a7a2d71203590d185cf4bd9..2e0795a71135b7472b361de63b8e930f6dc57d35 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/cuda_model.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/deepseek_v41/cuda_model.zig
@@ -434,7 +434,8 @@ pub const Model = struct {
         // TF_DSV41_SAMPLING=1: keyed sampling (T > 0) on every rank; off: such requests are refused (error.Sampling)
         m.sampler = if (samp.enabled()) try samp.GpuSampler.init(gpa, &m.f) else null;
         m.gt.sampler = m.sampler;
-        m.grammar_masks = try grammar.Masks.init(gpa, &m.f, @max(64, rows_cap));
+        // TF_DSV41_GRAMMAR (default on): structured output's masks on every rank; 0: such requests are refused
+        m.grammar_masks = if (try grammar.enabled()) try grammar.Masks.init(gpa, &m.f, @max(64, rows_cap)) else null;
         if (m.vision_config) |v| try vision.tower(gpa, io, &m.f, &m.pack, &m.driver, m.tcfg.rank, v.shape);
         try m.driver.synchronize();
         tr.step("end", cuda.usage(false));
